      Day 12 — Wednesday, February 18, 2026
    </header>

    <div class="intro">
      <h3 style="color: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 1rem;">🎿 Day 12 Overview</h3>
      <p>Wednesday is a blockbuster day with eleven medal events. The women's giant slalom graces Cortina's Olympia delle Tofane, the biathlon men's 20km individual — the sport's most gruelling format — unfolds at Anterselva, ice dance crowns its champions in the free dance, skeleton women determine their medallists, the short track mixed team relay delivers a chaotic multi-format final, bobsled two-man starts its opening runs, and freestyle skiing slopestyle decides its first gold. The cross-country women's 4×5km relay and speed skating men's 5000m add further drama.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="highlights">
      <h3>⭐ Day 12 Highlights</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Women's Giant Slalom — two-run duel on the Olympia delle Tofane in Cortina</li>
        <li>Biathlon Men's 20km Individual — the ultimate test of endurance and accuracy</li>
        <li>Figure Skating Ice Dance Free Dance — crowning the Olympic champion couple</li>
        <li>Skeleton Women's Final (Runs 3 &amp; 4) at Cesana</li>
        <li>Short Track Mixed Team Relay Final — frenetic multi-gender sprint</li>
        <li>Cross-Country Women's 4×5km Relay at Tesero</li>
        <li>Speed Skating Men's 5000m — Dutch dominance at Barentsburg Arena</li>
        <li>Freestyle Skiing Women's Slopestyle Final at Livigno</li>
        <li>Bobsled Two-Man — Opening Runs 1 &amp; 2 at Cesana</li>
        <li>Nordic Combined Individual Normal Hill / 10km at Predazzo &amp; Tesero</li>
        <li>Curling Round Robin continues at Cortina</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

